    **BAD (a checklist, no character):** "Square jaw, blunt chin. Gray eyes. Brown hair, shoulder-length. Rough skin. Broad-shouldered. No visible scars, tattoos, or birthmarks. Steel armor, iron helmet, leather boots. Recognizable by the brown hair and steel armor."

    **GOOD (an older Redguard man):** "A lean, sun-dark man in his fifties in travel-stained desert robes, his shaved scalp split by a long pale scar. His face is long and hollow-cheeked, with a hooked nose broken at least once, deep-set black eyes under a heavy brow, and thin lips half-hidden by his beard. A grizzled beard is trimmed close to the jaw; the scar runs from his crown down to his left ear, which is missing its lobe.

    He is wiry rather than broad, all tendon and knuckle, with a ropy scar across the back of one hand. He dresses for travel, not show: a dust-colored robe faded at the hems over a padded leather vest, a curved blade at his hip, and a red sash gone brown with age."

    Look carefully, then write the description.
